=== HOW TO READ THIS
  'ASan est' is wall x 38, the factor TD-032 measured on this suite. It is an
  EXTRAPOLATION from one measured point, not a measurement at that resolution, and
  the policy must say so. The cap it has to clear is ctest --timeout 7200 PER TEST.
  A row whose status is not Converged is NOT a candidate fixture at any price: a
  cheap case that stops exercising the reacting path tests nothing.

=== THE COMPARISON the audit section 5 said was missing
  Release measured: 100 cells 10.5 s, 150 cells 19.2 s (logs/01)
  The 'ASan est' column above is Release x 38 and is NOT this run; the wall column IS.
  Divide to get the REAL factor at each resolution, and compare the two factors to each
  other: if they differ a lot, the factor is resolution-dependent and the audit's
  extrapolation to other sizes is unsound.

